#!/bin/sh
# The guest's object converter, OBJCONVERT (tools/objconvert/
# ObjectConvert.Mod), as MACRO-32 to build it from, for tools/vax-do,
# tools/vax-run and tools/vax-assemble, which send poc's objects to the
# VAX/VMS development system (PLAN.md Phase 18 step 4c; doc/developer/
# vax-object-language.md, section 15.9, proposals 7 and 8). Writes, when
# they are missing or older than poc or the sources, the converter's
# modules' .mar, rtl/vax's PocRtl.mar, and the procedure poc -build
# writes, into <dir> (default build/objconvert), and prints a key, a
# checksum of them all: the guest builds the converter into the
# account's [.BIN] again whenever the key it keeps there differs
# (tools/vax-objconvert.tcl).
#
#   tools/vax-objconvert [<dir>]
#
# POC names the poc to use (default build/bin/poc). Runs at once share
# <dir>, so each holds a lock, the directory <dir>.lock, while it writes.
set -e

here=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
root=$(dirname "$here")
dir=${1:-$root/build/objconvert}
poc=${POC:-$root/build/bin/poc}
[ -x "$poc" ] || { echo "vax-objconvert: no poc at $poc" >&2; exit 2; }

# the key of the files in dir
key() {
  (cd "$1" && cat $(ls | LC_ALL=C sort) | cksum | awk '{ print $1 }')
}

# dir is up to date when its KEY is newer than poc and every source
fresh() {
  [ -f "$dir.key" ] || return 1
  [ -z "$(find "$poc" "$root/tools/objconvert" "$root/rtl/vax" -maxdepth 1 -newer "$dir.key" \( -name '*.Mod' -o -name '*.mar' -o -name poc \) 2>/dev/null)" ]
}

if ! fresh; then
  until mkdir "$dir.lock" 2>/dev/null; do sleep 1; done
  trap 'rmdir "$dir.lock"' EXIT
  if ! fresh; then
    new=$(mktemp -d "$dir.XXXXXX")
    # compiled as a copy, so that the procedure poc writes names no
    # directory of this host, and the key is the same from every checkout
    cp "$root/tools/objconvert/ObjectConvert.Mod" "$new/"
    (cd "$new" && "$poc" -target vax-dec-vms -import-path "$root/rtl/vax" -build ObjectConvert.Mod >log 2>&1) || {
      cat "$new/log" >&2; rm -rf "$new"; echo "vax-objconvert: the converter did not compile" >&2; exit 2
    }
    rm -f "$new"/*.sym "$new/log" "$new/ObjectConvert.Mod"
    cp "$root/rtl/vax/PocRtl.mar" "$new/PocRtl.mar"
    rm -rf "$dir"
    mv "$new" "$dir"
    key "$dir" >"$dir.key"
  fi
fi
cat "$dir.key"
